{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3445","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3445","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3445\",\"parent_revision\":\"bd70fa157810afdc365dfbe31acfba6953e53827cefa89e94192bcce3f12ec30\",\"root_revision\":\"bd70fa157810afdc365dfbe31acfba6953e53827cefa89e94192bcce3f12ec30\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe scanner that enforces plugin self-containment exempts every path built on a substitution variable, on a stated premise that is false.\\n\\nTHE PREMISE\\n\\nplugins/plugin-creator/skills/lint/scripts/audit_runtime_escapes.py, module docstring:\\n\\n  3. Load-time substitutions are portable. ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} and ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}\\n     resolve in any environment, so paths built on them are never reported.\\n\\nImplemented as _PORTABLE_PREFIXES at line 79 and applied at line 165, where a path starting with any of those prefixes returns False and is never counted as an escape.\\n\\nWHY IT IS FALSE\\n\\n\\\"Resolve in any environment\\\" does not hold. Verified against harness source and vendor documentation, 2026-09-06:\\n\\n- Codex performs no inline substitution anywhere. Its plugin MCP configuration contains zero CLAUDE_ references and no expansion; a reader receives the literal string. Codex exports CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT as an environment variable to hook processes only, which does nothing for a path written in prose.\\n- OpenCode and Crush read .claude/skills directories but perform no substitution.\\n- Cursor's ${VAR} syntax denotes admin-supplied secrets, not path substitution.\\n- Kimi substitutes ${KIMI_SKILL_DIR}, not the Claude Code variables.\\n- ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR} does not appear on Claude Code's plugins-reference page at all, and neither variable is documented as substituted inside references/*.md \u2014 canary testing in this repo on 2026-08-06, run twice, found no substitution there.\\n\\nIMPACT\\n\\nThe scanner silently passes the exact class of reference it exists to catch. A plugin whose skills reference ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs/x.md scores zero escapes and still breaks for any consumer on a harness that does not substitute. Because the check reports nothing, the failure surfaces as a missing file at runtime rather than as a finding.\\n\\nThis also means every escape count produced by this scanner understates the true number, including the counts recorded in the per-plugin items filed alongside it.\\n\\nSELF-CONTRADICTION IN THE SAME PLUGIN\\n\\nThree artifacts in plugin-creator hold three positions on the same variables. The scanner says they are portable and exempts them. plugins/plugin-creator/docs/runtime-environment.md says a substitution variable is \\\"a bet on which harness reads your skill\\\". Ten SKILL.md pointers in the plugin are themselves written as ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs/runtime-environment.md, so the plugin's own navigation depends on the bet its documentation warns against.\\n\\nAt most one of those three can be right, and nothing detects the disagreement.\\n\\nWHAT NEEDS DECIDING, NOT JUST FIXING\\n\\nRemoving the exemption would flag the plugin's own ten pointers and much of the repo. Keeping it requires a defensible statement of which harnesses the exemption assumes. The underlying question is whether these plugins target Claude Code with best-effort portability elsewhere, or target the Agent Skills standard with Claude Code as one consumer. The scanner currently encodes the first answer while the documentation argues the second.\\n\\nUser-provided context: found by asking what the documentation section was for rather than whether its facts were correct. Five rounds of fact-checking the same document never compared it against the code enforcing the same rule.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Objective reassessment of runtime-environment.md, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1db2b3ab9129f455b840a7abec027166a78e1ceaefd18bdcab5d9191fd7f1451\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSAmeA\"}"}